[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3737817722","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114877#issuecomment-3737817722","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114877","id":3737817722,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eypJ6","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-12T10:20:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-12T10:20:13Z","body":"Not sure types are usable in this way in GDScript, this doesn't check for two objects of these types, it produces two types and calls `new` on the *result*, this would be no different from:\n```gdscript\nvar x = (scene_a if cond else scene_b).instantiate()\n```\nI'd say\n\nGDScript doesn't have a first class type system so I don't expect this sort of thing to work","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3737817722/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_